This assertion checks if the return value of ArrayList.LastIndexOf() is negative. If it is, then it asserts that the old array's size should be at least -1. This is because the ArrayList.LastIndexOf() method in C# returns the last occurrence of a specified element or -1 if the element is not found in the ArrayList. As per the context, if it returns -1, the size of the original array (arrList), should be at least -1. So, this assertion verifies that this condition is true.--------------------Here is the solution:

```cs

Debug.Assert(New_Ret < 0 && Old_arrListCount - 1 > -1);

```

This "Debug.Assert" statement assures that the return value of "LastIndexOf" function is less than 0 and the size of the list is at least -1. 

Remember, "Debug.Assert" in C# is used for conditional compilation. When the .DEBUG symbol is set, assertions are checked. If they fail, the method System.Diagnostics.Debug.Assert(bool, string, string) throws an AssertFailedException. If the .DEBUG symbol is not set, the assertion is ignored. This allows for efficient checking in a Debug build.--------------------Here is the commented csharp code:

```csharp

