namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        public void PUT_LastIndexOfContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
        {
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);

            int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

            // @@@ If the return value is negative, old array's size is at least -1
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX < 0 || Old_arrListCount >= -Old_arrListIndexOfX - 1);
        }
    }
}

```
This line of code checks if the return value of LastIndexOf(x) is negative, or if the count of the array list is at least one less than the negative return value. This assures that the return value is indicating that the value of x is not in the array list, or that it is the new last one in the array list.--------------------Based on your requirement and comment "If the return value is negative, old array's size is at least -1", the debug statement I would create would be:
```cs
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount >= New_Ret - 1, "Old array's count is at least -1");
```
The comment is suggesting that in a case when LastIndexOf() return value is negative (or -1), then the old array should have one item less. So the assertion checks this condition.--------------------The assertions to make are about the conditions at two critical points. In the old state where the element is not there, and in the new state where the element may be there or not. This will cover the test for the case where the element does not exist in the array or it is the last such element.

